ntdll: Notify the ARM64EC emulator about non-image section protections.

New executable data-section mappings were absent from FEX's executable
intervals: VirtualQuery reported PAGE_EXECUTE_READ, but the first call
faulted as non-executable. The map helper only reached its notification
path during image loading, and then only for image sections.

Report successful non-image mappings through the existing paired memory
protection callbacks. Keep loader-only image notifications unchanged.
Both NtMapViewOfSection and NtMapViewOfSectionEx use this helper. No new
emulator export or game-specific behavior is required.

Regression: tests/x64-fidelity/memtest.c, code.mapped_alias_flush.
M4 control: 50 pass / 1 fail, execute AV on the first call.
Patched: 51/0 in normal and full validation modes; context 546/0.
Native Windows reference and FH6 gameplay verification remain pending.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -834,9 +834,20 @@
     SECTION_IMAGE_INFORMATION info;
     NTSTATUS status;
 
+    if (!pNotifyMapViewOfSection && !pNotifyMemoryProtect) return;
+    if (NtQuerySection( handle, SectionImageInformation, &info, sizeof(info), NULL ))
+    {
+        /* Data-section mappings can also contain x64 code. They do not receive
+         * image notifications; report their protection to the emulator. */
+        if (pNotifyMemoryProtect)
+        {
+            pNotifyMemoryProtect( addr, size, protect, FALSE, 0 );
+            pNotifyMemoryProtect( addr, size, protect, TRUE, STATUS_SUCCESS );
+        }
+        return;
+    }
     if (!pNotifyMapViewOfSection) return;
     if (!NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.ArbitraryUserPointer) return;
-    if (NtQuerySection( handle, SectionImageInformation, &info, sizeof(info), NULL )) return;
     status = pNotifyMapViewOfSection( NULL, addr, NULL, size, alloc, protect );
     if (NT_SUCCESS(status)) return;
     NtUnmapViewOfSection( GetCurrentProcess(), addr );
